From 13fe76b674cc627ab4577f8c41dd3602526c10fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Yu <josephyu@yahooinc.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:32:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Cap the message log at 16kB, not 100kB

LogRotate defaults to 100kB across 25 files. Measured on a device that had
filled most of it: 58331 bytes held 788 messages, so entries average 74 bytes
and the default allows roughly 1400.

That is too many for two separate reasons, both observed on hardware.

Restoring runs one message per UI tick, from ViewController::runOnce, so 788
messages took 38.7 seconds of every single boot - and while the device was
crash-looping every 55 seconds it spent most of its life in that loop.

Worse, the restore creates an LVGL object per message, and at 788 it ran the
LVGL heap out. newMessageContainer then returned null and newMessage called
lv_obj_create on the null parent:

    0x4201e3e3 lv_obj_class_create_obj
    0x4201e4a1 lv_obj_create
    0x42087335 TFTView_320x240::newMessage
    0x42089bd1 TFTView_320x240::restoreMessage
    0x420880e6 ViewController::restoreTextMessages

That also explains why the device got worse over time rather than breaking
suddenly: the log grows across reboots and never shrinks on its own, so it
crept up on the limit.

16kB over 8 files is about 220 messages - roughly 11 seconds to restore, and
well clear of where it broke. Set at the call site rather than in LogRotate's
defaults, since it is a policy choice by the caller. maxFileSize stays several
times sizeof(LogMessage), which init() depends on when deciding to rotate.

Both init() and write() enforce the quota, so an existing oversized log trims
itself down rather than needing to be cleared by hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjqMrWWLWXvmh69rvGCEo
---
 source/graphics/common/ViewController.cpp | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/graphics/common/ViewController.cpp b/source/graphics/common/ViewController.cpp
index 451aa19..d7d216d 100644
--- a/source/graphics/common/ViewController.cpp
+++ b/source/graphics/common/ViewController.cpp
@@ -21,7 +21,19 @@ constexpr const char *logDir = "/messages";
  *
  */
 ViewController::ViewController()
-    : view(nullptr), log(persistentFS, logDir, sizeof(LogMessage)), client(nullptr), sendId(1), myNodeNum(0), setupDone(false),
+    // Message log quota, overriding LogRotate's 100kB/25-file default. Measured
+    // on a device that had filled it: 58331 bytes held 788 messages, so entries
+    // average 74 bytes and the default allows roughly 1400.
+    //
+    // That is too many for two reasons. Restoring is one message per UI tick, so
+    // 788 took 38.7 seconds of every boot. And the restore creates an LVGL
+    // object per message; at 788 it exhausted the LVGL heap, newMessageContainer
+    // returned null, and lv_obj_create panicked on the null parent.
+    //
+    // 16kB / 8 files is about 220 messages - roughly 11 seconds to restore and
+    // well clear of where it broke. maxFileSize stays several times sizeof
+    // (LogMessage), which init() relies on when it decides to rotate.
+    : view(nullptr), log(persistentFS, logDir, sizeof(LogMessage), 16384, 8, 2048), client(nullptr), sendId(1), myNodeNum(0), setupDone(false),
       configCompleted(false), messagesRestored(false), requestConfigRequired(true)
 {
 }
